A||N||2||glava2876||84 2.5 fuel problems||||5||
Z||000000||glava2876||04-21-2001||09:12 PM||||Just a reminder, this car hadn't been started in about 10 years -but it only has 37,000 miles. I put in some fresh gas, dry gas, injector cleaner etc.Then I put in new plugs and fuel filter and it started -but wouldn't idle. The cap and rotor looked crappy inside, so I replaced them and the wires. The car started and idled great, BUT, would stumble and stall when I steped on the gas. I had it idling for 8-10 minutes while I was checking things out -it stalled and won't start. I pulled the fuel line from the filter and it is pumping fuel -into a jug while I crank it and it isn't gunky. But it didn't seem to have high pressure when I disconnected the line. A little gas in the TBI and it starts for a few seconds. What is the best sequence to determining what to do next? Can the fuel pump move fuel, but be too weak to maintain pressure? I don't want to pull the tank unless it is the only was to check out the pump.Can the pressure regulator stick and do wierd things? Any help will be GREATLY appreciated. Thanks, Glen      ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-21-2001||09:16 PM||||Yes, both those things can happen. You'll need to put a pressure gauge on the TBI inlet and see what is going on.<P>A very quick test you could try pinching a rubber section of the return line. That might get pressure up if the regulator is shot.||||reg||1
Z||000002||glava2876||04-21-2001||09:27 PM||||Thanks, I'll try that. The pinching will make it run? If that happens replace the fuel regulator? If not replace the pump? Thanks again, Glen||||reg||1
